{{- /*
  beads-issues/ensure-bead-branch — headless branch creation for automated
  loop drivers. Supports one branch per bead or one shared branch per epic.

  Called before the FIRST commit of a bead (fix-phase entry / implement-phase
  entry). Must be idempotent — a feature bead crosses four phases in four
  separate turns and re-enters this fragment each time.

  Composes git/shared/identify-remote-branch to resolve <target-remote> and
  <target-base> (that fragment already has a non-prompting scheduled-mode
  branch, so nothing here needs its own loop gate).

  Unlike git/shared/ensure-feature-branch (interactive-first: refuses to
  branch in scheduled mode, uses mitto_ui_form otherwise), this fragment is
  headless-only by construction — one code path, no UI tools, safe in both
  interactive and scheduled runs.

  Callers pass a dict:
    "Ctx"    — the full render context (`.`), forwarded verbatim to the
               nested identify-remote-branch call so its own .Session.IsLoop
               gate still sees the real session.
    "Target" — the resolved bead ID. Required.
    "Type"   — conventional branch-type prefix: "feat" for features, "fix"
               for bugs. Empty string renders `<type>`.

  Reads Ctx.Args.FromBranch (default "main") and Ctx.Args.GroupEpics
  (default-on; only "false" disables it).

  After this block, the caller can refer to `<branch-name>` as the resolved,
  already-checked-out feature branch.
*/ -}}
{{- $ctx := .Ctx -}}
{{- $target := .Target -}}
{{- $type := .Type -}}{{- if eq $type "" }}{{ $type = "<type>" }}{{ end -}}
{{- $fromBranch := Default "main" $ctx.Args.FromBranch -}}
{{- $groupEpics := ne $ctx.Args.GroupEpics "false" -}}
{{ template "git/shared/identify-remote-branch" $ctx }}

For this workflow, the explicit base is `{{ $fromBranch }}`; use it as
`<target-branch>` even when the repository's default branch differs.

#### Resolve the branch owner and name

The branch name must be **stable across phases** — this fragment is re-entered
once per phase, so derive it deterministically.{{ if $groupEpics }} If the target's direct parent is
an `epic`, set `branch_target` to that epic so every sibling shares one branch;
otherwise keep the task itself.{{ end }}

```bash
branch_target="{{ $target }}"
branch_type="{{ $type }}"
{{ if $groupEpics -}}
parent=$(bd show {{ $target }} --json | jq -r '.[0].parent // empty')
if [ -n "$parent" ] && [ "$(bd show "$parent" --json | jq -r '.[0].issue_type // empty')" = "epic" ]; then
  branch_target="$parent"
  branch_type="epic"
fi
{{- end }}
slug=$(bd show "$branch_target" --json | jq -r '.[0].title' \
  | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]' | sed -E 's/[^a-z0-9]+/-/g; s/^-+|-+$//g' \
  | cut -c1-40 | sed -E 's/-+$//')
branch="${branch_type}/${branch_target}-$slug"
```

#### Ensure the branch exists and is checked out

Idempotent — safe to re-run every phase:

```bash
current=$(git branch --show-current)
if [ "$current" = "$branch" ]; then
  : # already on it — no-op
elif git show-ref --verify --quiet "refs/heads/$branch"; then
  git switch "$branch"
else
  base_branch={{ $fromBranch | printf "%q" }}
  git fetch <target-remote> "$base_branch"
  git switch -c "$branch" "<target-remote>/$base_branch"
fi
```

Never create the new branch from bare `HEAD`: a prior task may have left a
different task branch checked out. Existing deterministic branches are reused
only for later phases{{ if $groupEpics }} or later children of the same epic{{ end }}.

No `mitto_ui_*` calls anywhere in this fragment — safe for unattended runs.
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
